(4788133, 689558, 47906, '<td valign="top">Hey Peter,<br/> <br/>Excellent lighting and very origonal idea on this shot. Very great control. I am sure that your wife will absolutely love this. Also Congrats on a new PB. I am sure this one will be tuff to beat. Excellent job.<br/> <br/>Rich</td>', 'Hey Peter, Excellent lighting and very origonal idea on this shot. Very great control. I am sure that your wife will absolutely love this. Also Congrats on a new PB. I am sure this one will be tuff to beat. Excellent job. Rich', '2008-06-27 14:45:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4788223, 689114, 63972, '<td valign="top">Wow, thanks for all the nice comments.  I was not expecting the 5th place to be honest and I did not actually shot this for the challenge. I was trying my new 70-200 2.8L IS and just got this shot by chance. If I was shotting it for the challenge probably I would have gone with an f/2.8 to get even more shallow dof.<br/> <br/>Some self critique:<br/> <br/>- I have to agree that this is not a portrait shot per se, but looks like most of the people are ok with that ;-)<br/> <br/>- I really wanted to get a color version for the challenge but just couldn''t get the colors right with the jpeg version.  So I ended up going with bw... Color version has a bit more 3d effect. Lesson''s learned:  Will go back to shooting raw or at least try to use the right white balance; never use the autobalance when shooting jpeg at all...  Well, I''m glad again most of the people liked the bw version.<br/> <br/>Thanks again everybody for the comments and votes.  And the biggest thanks go to my beautiful twin daughters of course...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-27 16:08:18.</i></td>', 'Wow, thanks for all the nice comments.  I was not expecting the 5th place to be honest and I did not actually shot this for the challenge. I was trying my new 70-200 2.8L IS and just got this shot by chance. If I was shotting it for the challenge probably I would have gone with an f/2.8 to get even more shallow dof. Some self critique: - I have to agree that this is not a portrait shot per se, but looks like most of the people are ok with that ;-) - I really wanted to get a color version for the challenge but just couldn''t get the colors right with the jpeg version.  So I ended up going with bw... Color version has a bit more 3d effect. Lesson''s learned:  Will go back to shooting raw or at least try to use the right white balance; never use the autobalance when shooting jpeg at all...  Well, I''m glad again most of the people liked the bw version. Thanks again everybody for the comments and votes.  And the biggest thanks go to my beautiful twin daughters of course...', '2008-06-27 17:06:57.000000', '2008-06-27 17:08:18.000000', 0),
(4788247, 689558, 74979, '<td valign="top">very well done!  I liked this in the challenge too, nice originality and the lighting works so well<br/> <br/></td>', 'very well done!  I liked this in the challenge too, nice originality and the lighting works so well ', '2008-06-27 17:44:35.000000', NULL, 0),
